  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-02-03T23:06:36.329Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The current VRChat menu layout works well and does not need to be redesigned. However, the way players interact with it feels disconnected from the rest of the VR experience.\n\nIn VR, players constantly use their hands to gesture, point, and express themselves, but when opening the menu, interaction switches to laser pointers and button presses. It would be really cool if VR players could also interact with the existing menu by physically touching it with their hands or fingers.\n\nFor example, instead of only aiming a laser, players could reach out and tap buttons, press toggles, or interact with sliders directly using their avatar’s hands, similar to how interaction works in games like Rec Room.\n\nThis would not require changing how the menu looks or where anything is placed. The layout, options, and behavior could stay the same, with physical touch acting as an additional interaction method alongside the current controls.\n\nBeing able to physically touch the menu would make it feel more immersive and natural, helping the menu feel like part of the world rather than something separate from the player’s body.\n\nOverall, this would help the VRChat menu better match the physical, embodied experience that VRChat already encourages.",
